        "text": "Page: Abraham Bankier. Sentence: Abraham Bankier (1910-1956) was one of the owners of the \"Rekord\" factory on Lipowa street in Cracow, Poland, that Oskar Schindler took over during World War II.\nPage: Oskar Schindler. Sentence: Oskar Schindler (28 April 1908 – 9 October 1974) was a German industrialist, spy, and member of the Nazi Party who is credited with saving the lives of 1,200 Jews during the Holocaust by employing them in his enamelware and ammunitions factories, which were located in occupied Poland and the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia.",
